# == Buffet ==

# The Cargo workspace's build output. Cargo.lock is NOT ignored: the
# workspace holds runners, so the lockfile is committed from the first build
# that resolves alonzo from crates.io (HOUSE.2), and not before, since a lock
# made under the local patch below would name a path and not the registry.
target/

# Local overrides of Cargo's configuration: .cargo/config.toml holds, until
# alonzo 0.1.0 is on crates.io (HOUSE.2), a [patch.crates-io] that satisfies
# Cargo.toml's registry pin from the engine's tree beside this repository. It
# is the owner's machine's and never the repository's.
.cargo/

# The page tools/build_web.ps1 will write from the vendored template and the
# engine's module (HOUSE.4): the template is source, the filled page is
# output.
web/index.html

# Scratch area for throwaway experiments, so they never clutter history.
scratch/

# Editor and operating-system residue.
~$*
*.tmp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
